### PyCharm / VS Code REST Client: click the run arrow next to a request.
@api = http://localhost:5080
@key = lab-dev-key

### Health
GET {{api}}/api/health

### Loan products
GET {{api}}/api/products

### Quote a loan (nothing is saved)
POST {{api}}/api/loans/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "PERS", "amount": 10000, "months": 12 }

### All loans (paged)
GET {{api}}/api/loans?status=active&page=1&size=20

### One loan
GET {{api}}/api/loans/1

### Its repayment schedule
GET {{api}}/api/loans/1/schedule

### Its event history
GET {{api}}/api/loans/1/events

### Open a loan (needs the API key)
POST {{api}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "customerName": "Ana Pop", "productCode": "PERS", "amount": 10000, "months": 12 }

### Repay (needs the API key and an Idempotency-Key). Send it twice: 201, then 200.
POST {{api}}/api/loans/1/repayments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
Idempotency-Key: try-it-1

{ "amount": 500 }

### Open without the key: expect 401
POST {{api}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "No Key", "productCode": "PERS", "amount": 10000, "months": 12 }

### Amount above the product maximum: expect 400
POST {{api}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "customerName": "Too High", "productCode": "PERS", "amount": 50000.01, "months": 12 }

### Portfolio statistics (slow with many loans: lesson 07)
GET {{api}}/api/stats/portfolio
